      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "2eb9b1d1419b4e9a1921cc32459169c47078111c",
            "subject": "LU-9 lod: allocate MDT stripes by weighted round-robin"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-09-29 17:15:17.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-06 00:43:51.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-9 lod: show the round-robin allocator state",
        "message": "LU-9 lod: show the round-robin allocator state\n\nThe weights of the targets shown by lod.*.qos_ost_weights don't\nexplain which target the allocator chooses, since that depends on the\norder of the round-robin array, its start index and offset, and the\nfailure domains and servers of the targets.\n\nAdd svr_id, tgt_active, failure_domain and rr_slot, the slot of the\ntarget in the round-robin array, to lod.*.qos_ost_weights,\nlod.*.qos_mdt_weights and the pool qos_ost_weights files.  Add\nlod.*.qos_rr_state, lod.*.mdt_qos_rr_state and the pool qos_rr_state\nfiles to show the round-robin array in allocation order and the start\nindex, offset and weighted round-robin laps of each allocation stream.\nReading them takes lq_rw_sem so that rr_slot matches the array, and\ncan wait while QoS allocation holds it.\n\nAlso fix writing lod.*.qos_mdt_weights, which reset the MDT penalties\nunder the OST lq_rw_sem and marked the OST QoS data dirty instead of\nthe MDT data.\n\nAdd a man page for lod.qos_rr_state and sanity test_51j to check the\narray slots, the streams and leaving out an inactive OST.\n\nFixes: a44956f0d57d (\"LU-16501 lod: add qos_ost_weights to debugfs\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I6c824dc4dc3124976ddd3aa6f3e16cb9d13ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
